{"allowed_english": [], "context": {"approved_glossary_entries": [], "generation_contexts": [{"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:groupoids-quotients:inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0001", "hash": "sha256:18252b43b49a9ea070da6dd6872e63426c72e436294de248f5f230f3201ff6a1", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 14454, "byte_start": 14152, "file": "groupoids-quotients.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:4cf83ec77e18c4535476f944577cf60969d776c125082cb94d5b699e1b9ef487", "line_end": 422, "line_start": 416}, "owner_tag": "048M", "parent_tag": "048M", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$j = (t, s) : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0002": "$j$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$t(s^{-1}(\\{u\\}))$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$j$", "MATH_0008": "$R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b7d5e0905dfb596c0813e525e0900a7d9720fc20c953e8ff042ad33f45bf59c7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a0d261c9c3a8703de72105146a0f3b66c4100ce34f608d3734cecbd5fb44af06", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a pre-relation.\nIf <MATH_0002> is a pre-equivalence relation, then loosely speaking\nthe ``orbits'' of <MATH_0003> on <MATH_0004>\nare the subsets <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006>. However, if <MATH_0007> is just a\npre-relation, then we need to take the equivalence relation generated\nby <MATH_0008>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6786495e1073be55f3abc005ffba20fb2d91e8282813afe673b011d6de0dff30", "unit_id": "inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:groupoids-quotients:inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0002", "hash": "sha256:97da7186a2ebb6d114ab70f180d4fe650849fe0c8537e12e7abc14fe969be73d", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 15396, "byte_start": 15107, "file": "groupoids-quotients.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:d3254266640d34d06a6eefd1cd50cc7bbecde98bdede4f7c4e60f0d0e4c0e28f", "line_end": 452, "line_start": 447}, "owner_tag": "048M", "parent_tag": "048M", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u' \\in O_u$", "MATH_0002": "$u \\in O_{u'}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-groupoids-lemma-pre-equivalence-equivalence-relation-points}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3f0a7f7be2259564f456834e2ff99b88650ff27a90bfe93f28c8c16d332e5b1f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7a2837356eda55c164ab8d7e7645960b0aeab6c2f5bcf3309c1769c334639a80", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIt is clear that these are the equivalence classes of an equivalence relation,\ni.e., we have <MATH_0001> if and only if <MATH_0002>. The following lemma\nis a reformulation of\nGroupoids in Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d47fa554c986ddcfa3fbd9449b402953e48498b930cd6a0a705d7ec2269aaefb", "unit_id": "inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0002"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:groupoids-quotients:inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0006", "hash": "sha256:aa7f3957ee0a5822861d2487ccb13afb494806f1474a04e5c79675dc14b7a436", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 20038, "byte_start": 19829, "file": "groupoids-quotients.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:025071b3500415c9460a714b88eeda59373581a748c2b22e3e0cd7ef7292242e", "line_end": 561, "line_start": 558}, "owner_tag": "048M", "parent_tag": "048M", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-geometric-orbits}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:42350055aa05d8f348f4b4d70abb962851050d4faf4e17a248f245001db5bb2a", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIt turns out that in good cases orbits and weak orbits agree, see\nLemma <REF_0001>. The following lemma illustrates\nthe difference in the special case of a pre-equivalence relation.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6ec16e1ebf21b87696483180e4f7063c655c80eafe6d4f9fd57efac0a4af9de3", "unit_id": "inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0006"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:groupoids-quotients:inventory:groupoids-quotients:048R:proof/0001", "hash": "sha256:126e450c7b1ad8bed67e4643e65c31acb4b8e09513d936d678f208081967db75", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 20858, "byte_start": 20695, "file": "groupoids-quotients.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:e167294d263d9364cc688f016af8e83b0e136f4ba2a750f775ebf7d6d24dd104", "line_end": 590, "line_start": 587}, "owner_tag": "048R", "parent_tag": "048M", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$j(R(k)) \\subset U(k) \\times U(k)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c2bcedc4a7477ac8d4f52471a4e04ff798dfd18898b6d65d9ff961a37bc8a637", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e23c7e5470ea473ba76e474915e310e4e9cc1ed84f1690f1dbdead47cbc72eff", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is true because by definition of a pre-equivalence relation the image\n<MATH_0001> is an equivalence relation.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:95e4a0a7bcd4b4d28e81f1e2bd35a03b85800bd7a181fe7cce2bac035508030c", "unit_id": "inventory:groupoids-quotients:048R:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:groupoids-quotients:inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0011", "hash": "sha256:2974f4612da1a6878c406823cc083c13156b8cb8d84a603411860581fd46a231", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 29778, "byte_start": 29383, "file": "groupoids-quotients.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:a076b59690a9db71faba5e49e29c3ea9622a48dc72179a5d2cda95991f92c2df", "line_end": 845, "line_start": 839}, "owner_tag": "048M", "parent_tag": "048M", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Y \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c149022db57b1cf4a005738a622d6d49174685360ccdd299a3d6ff2abae3c2d6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5ba1d3557bcb19b307a4b409b3ddc5ddb426084e48346c6fc954c131190a30e1", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThe example above is instructive because the map <MATH_0001> even separates\norbits. It shows that in the category of algebraic spaces there are simply\ntoo many set-theoretically invariant morphisms lying around. Next, let us\ndefine what it means for <MATH_0002> to be a set-theoretic equivalence relation, while\nremembering that we need to allow for field extensions to make this work\ncorrectly.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1c42c506360aa4f11a62b5526a13428802d3c756d47f114fe714a7f94dda5344", "unit_id": "inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0011"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:groupoids-quotients:inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0012", "hash": "sha256:729e5aebb0f1086d72c8cf8d0d5047c2057716f733c18a0d55d76bdfc616152d", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 30597, "byte_start": 30539, "file": "groupoids-quotients.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:4265bb8b07a3a72ca7d17c323e723d77d6543248869c069ee116e8acdbb1c1e8", "line_end": 871, "line_start": 870}, "owner_tag": "048M", "parent_tag": "048M", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2d86ee44b67c4ca5ad8e855f2a695885e8ef58959cc7b7f8ce73a9a526a1ab75", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nLet us reformulate this in more geometric terms.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:73955a882396716926ee36751c53f840704e30dc7668bf2a1e2a2107270874f9", "unit_id": "inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0012"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:groupoids-quotients:inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0015", "hash": "sha256:42b0650f9eefb283c4e9b495aeeb40a912d626966aa09e38f6e12653739a51c3", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 43711, "byte_start": 43358, "file": "groupoids-quotients.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:5c0456392f650e1df137255657b6898e0c3d20a000e10d471080b4348c009361", "line_end": 1180, "line_start": 1175}, "owner_tag": "048M", "parent_tag": "048M", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$s, t$", "MATH_0002": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$U(k) \\to X(k)$", "MATH_0004": "$k$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:598968d451a89290d068045e4cb796f36849ccc97587715ce81185c4b42f99a9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:22396514f428f18732fa5bf78e897b98d21782934e0a993c1a74500c71b488b9", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the following lemma it is (probably) not good enough to assume just that\nthe morphisms <MATH_0001> are locally of finite type. The reason is that\nit may happen that some map <MATH_0002> is an orbit space, yet is\nnot locally of finite type. In that case <MATH_0003> may not\nbe surjective for all algebraically closed fields <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a17a06e8605d7757e4bb24cd746e85e55870881069eb5f3a525b254ec7cc5e01", "unit_id": "inventory:groupoids-quotients:048M:paragraph/0015"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:groupoids-quotients:inventory:groupoids-quotients:04A0:proof/0001", "hash": "sha256:826c802a9f3f58f6577e86c921688ac0c0245794fce7eb708d62c9de27501cd5", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 45729, "byte_start": 44271, "file": "groupoids-quotients.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:66d0c7fd1a963640263354a3ecd5af229e8658bf5763c636d1262cffef6ccfb6", "line_end": 1224, "line_start": 1197}, "owner_tag": "04A0", "parent_tag": "048M", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$s, t, j, \\phi$", "MATH_0005": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0006": "$k$", "MATH_0007": "$B$", "MATH_0008": "$\\overline{x} \\in X(k)$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\times_{\\phi, X, \\overline{x}} \\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0010": "$k$", "MATH_0011": "$k$", "MATH_0012": "$\\overline{u}, \\overline{u}' \\in U(k)$", "MATH_0013": "$X(k)$", "MATH_0014": "$\\overline{u}, \\overline{u}'$", "MATH_0015": "$R$", "MATH_0016": "$j(R(k))$", "MATH_0017": "$k$", "MATH_0018": "$B$", "MATH_0019": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0020": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0021": "$R$", "MATH_0022": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0023": "$\\phi$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-permanence-finite-type}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-locally-finite-type-surjective-geometric-points}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{definition-set-theoretically-invariant}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-geometric-orbits}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:389e33f1dde4c2533c6ca5c8953a32ff20f28860ce7d8b7ce2e2e8d2cbdbc824", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ef5fc610af9b8a8a7955cf43a8b26ce13ca097e09cf9a7a94af5cacc584984c4", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that since <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> are locally of finite type over <MATH_0003> all of the\nmorphisms <MATH_0004> are locally of finite type, see\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nWe will also use without further mention\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0002>.\nAssume <MATH_0005> is an orbit space. Let <MATH_0006> be any algebraically closed\nfield over <MATH_0007>. Let <MATH_0008>. Consider\n<MATH_0009>.\nThis is a nonempty algebraic space\nwhich is locally of finite type over <MATH_0010>. Hence it has a <MATH_0011>-valued point.\nThis shows the displayed map of the lemma is surjective.\nSuppose that <MATH_0012> map to the same\nelement of <MATH_0013>. By\nDefinition <REF_0003>\nthis means that <MATH_0014> are in the same\n<MATH_0015>-orbit. By Lemma <REF_0004> this means that\nthey are equivalent under the equivalence relation generated by\n<MATH_0016>. Thus the displayed morphism is injective.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nConversely, assume the displayed map is bijective for all algebraically\nclosed fields <MATH_0017> over <MATH_0018>. This condition clearly implies that <MATH_0019>\nis surjective. We have already assumed that <MATH_0020> is <MATH_0021>-invariant.\nFinally, the injectivity of all the displayed maps implies that\n<MATH_0022> separates orbits. Hence <MATH_0023> is an orbit space.\n<STRUCT_0004>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:64a8d97df5e678bdae5a82caa068c9f8aa8ddb2d96f20ef28dc4ce5a1be40ad0", "unit_id": "inventory:groupoids-quotients:04A0:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:groupoids-quotients:inventory:groupoids-quotients:04A2:definition/0001", "hash": "sha256:2972e88304169e0c1200f32273208af6153c56b6626ab3c026ce865be1be54c5", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 46548, "byte_start": 45927, "file": "groupoids-quotients.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:74a7e78acb41e0e1c69247221af2497776e52682b44c23644db561ce4ea55a62", "line_end": 1258, "line_start": 1242}, "owner_tag": "04A2", "parent_tag": "04A1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04A1", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{definition-coarse}", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$j : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$B$", "MATH_0007": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0008": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0009": "$S = B$", "MATH_0010": "$U$", "MATH_0011": "$R$", "MATH_0012": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0014": "$\\phi$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{definition}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0006": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\item", "STRUCT_0009": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0010": "\\end{definition}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4435635741752cc3f6c6c4d21372a9f63e34ba4e03b8c8687d40390507d8898e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:09e3de996bc0b2273e26e6c8f3c022f336b40006590906f4ccc3d27624670c39", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme and <MATH_0002> an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a pre-relation.\nA morphism <MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>\nis called a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>coarse quotient<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0007> is a categorical quotient, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0008> is an orbit space.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nIf <MATH_0009>, <MATH_0010>, <MATH_0011> are all schemes, then we say a morphism of schemes\n<MATH_0012> is a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>coarse quotient in schemes<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<STRUCT_0007> <MATH_0013> is a categorical quotient in schemes, and\n<STRUCT_0008> <MATH_0014> is an orbit space.\n<STRUCT_0009>\n<STRUCT_0010>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:72717eadb5a4c115a766dc5026116f12f3a6e2ed9d498f33712296c0717d7f7c", "unit_id": "inventory:groupoids-quotients:04A2:definition/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:groupoids-quotients:inventory:groupoids-quotients:04A3:section_title/0001", "hash": "sha256:fcd438074460c066413e9f7475c7094f56bc85e2fc5bbfa765ce032dc8307e7a", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 47135, "byte_start": 47075, "file": "groupoids-quotients.tex